            "description": "Head/Header/Top; Foot/Footer/Bottom; Left/Right; Anchor X/Y or pair. Explicit pair overrides individual anchors.",
            "pattern": "<(?:(?:HEAD|HEADER|TOP|FOOT|FOOTER|BOTTOM|LEFT|RIGHT)|ANCHOR [XY]: \\d+\\.?\\d*|ANCHOR: \\d+\\.?\\d*, \\d+\\.?\\d*)>",
            "examples": [
                "<Anchor: 0.5, 1.0>"
            ],
            "context": "Author in Database Animations > Name (Animations.json name). Runtime reads the tag from that field; CLI writes it without executing the game or authored JavaScript. Anchor numbers are nonnegative ratios without a 0..1 clamp. X is ratio*sprite.width measured from the target sprite local origin (0 is that origin, not automatically its left edge); Y is (ratio-1)*(sprite.height*sprite.scale.y), so 0 is top and 1 is foot. An explicit pair overrides individual axis tags. The resulting point is transformed through the target sprite world transform. Head/Top and Foot/Bottom choose vertical bounds; Left/Right choose -width/2 or +width/2.",
