            "availability": "supported",
            "description": "X/Y locks accept finite numeric offsets or bare tags. Bare lock uses the configured offset and wins over explicit values.",
            "pattern": "<SCROLL LOCK [XY](?:: [+-]?(?:\\d+(?:\\.\\d*)?|\\.\\d+))?>",
            "examples": [
                "<Scroll Lock X: 0.5>"
            ],
            "context": "Author in Map Properties > Note (MapNNN.json note). Runtime reads the tag from that field; CLI writes it without executing the game or authored JavaScript. Camera locks use map display coordinates in tiles, not screen pixels. Automatic locking applies on a non-looping axis only when the viewport covers a fractional tile count whose ceiling equals the map size. Map notes <SCROLL LOCK X> / <SCROLL LOCK Y> select the configured DisplayLock value; <SCROLL LOCK X: 0.5> / <SCROLL LOCK Y: 0.5> select an explicit tile coordinate. A bare tag takes precedence if both forms occur. Locks are applied while screen zoom scale is 1; map setup refreshes the derived rules.",
